    id: 12,
    topic: "Computers",
    text: `Technology has transformed the way we work and communicate. Today we'll focus on computer-related collocations.

When you start your computer, you <b>boot up the computer</b>. If your computer <b>crashes</b>, you may need to <b>restart the system</b>. It's always important to <b>save your work</b> regularly to avoid losing data. You should also <b>back up your files</b> (save copies of your files in a separate location) in case of a system failure.

The internet has become essential for modern life. We <b>browse the internet</b> (look through websites without a specific goal), <b>search for information</b> online, and <b>download files</b> from websites. Many people also <b>upload content</b> to social media or video platforms.

Security is an important concern. It's vital to <b>install antivirus software</b> to protect against malware. You should use a <b>strong password</b> and never <b>click on suspicious links</b> or open emails from unknown senders, as these could be <b>phishing attacks</b>.

In the workplace, people often need to <b>send emails</b>, <b>attend virtual meetings</b>, and <b>share documents</b> online. <b>Cloud computing</b> allows people to <b>store data</b> remotely and <b>access files</b> from any device.

When technology doesn't work as expected, we say the system has a <b>technical glitch</b> or is <b>running slow</b>. You may need to <b>update the software</b> or <b>clear the cache</b> to improve performance.`,
